WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:01.430
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.162
today's message is it's possible.

00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:06.186
Over to you, Sierra.

00:00:06.186 --> 00:00:08.081
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.081 --> 00:00:10.998
(upbeat rap music)

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:20.164
- I hope to inspire others,

00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:23.028
and for people to know that
dreams are really real.

00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:25.857
You know, I wasn't raised
in this, every mistake,

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:27.271
every performance I've done

00:00:27.271 --> 00:00:29.140
is pretty much happened from the world.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.092
Or, like, I kid you not, I didn't grow up

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:34.252
doing singing in churches, I
didn't grow up doing anything,

00:00:34.252 --> 00:00:36.412
but I had a dream to do this,

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:38.526
and as soon as I put my mind to it

00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:41.037
and said this is what I want to
do, I wrote it down on paper,

00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:43.544
and I kid you not, everything manifested,

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:44.563
everything fell in place.

00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:47.874
So, I feel like my experience
can encourage anybody

00:00:47.874 --> 00:00:49.693
to know that no matter what time,

00:00:49.693 --> 00:00:52.718
you could be later on in
your time and you figure out

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.427
what you want to do, it's possible.

00:00:54.427 --> 00:00:55.897
So, I hope to inspire.

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:57.840
- The difference between whether
you will achieve your goals

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.475
or not quite often is whether
you believe you can or not.

00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:01.957
So, there's a famous Henry Ford quote,

00:01:01.957 --> 00:01:05.081
whether you believe you can
or you can't, you're right.

00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:08.266
And quite often what we do is
we don't listen to ourselves,

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:10.122
we listen to the people around us.

00:01:10.122 --> 00:01:11.360
Whenever you come up with a new idea,

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.899
what's the thing that we like to do?

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:14.082
We like to tell people about it,

00:01:14.082 --> 00:01:15.982
we tell our friends, we tell our family.

00:01:15.982 --> 00:01:19.123
And quite often, they tell
us it's a stupid idea,

00:01:19.123 --> 00:01:22.848
why are you doing this, you
didn't go to school for this,

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:24.174
you don't have the money to do this,

00:01:24.174 --> 00:01:25.872
and all of the limiting
beliefs that come in

00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:27.901
that then hold you back
from doing the thing

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.818
that you think is possible.

00:01:29.818 --> 00:01:31.215
And sometimes it's out of jealousy,

00:01:31.215 --> 00:01:33.273
'cause they tried to do
something and it never took off

00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:34.986
for them, so you're not allowed to do it.

00:01:34.986 --> 00:01:37.304
Sometimes it's out of love,
because they don't see the world

00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:39.190
the same way that you see the world.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.354
What's most important, though,

00:01:40.354 --> 00:01:42.834
is that if you're taking
advice from somebody,

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:45.037
it's somebody who's done
what you're trying to do.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.079
You know, if your parents or
your friends are the people

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:49.223
who are saying the reason that
it's not going to work out,

00:01:49.223 --> 00:01:51.387
but they've never done
what you're trying to do,

00:01:51.387 --> 00:01:53.743
their advice isn't helpful to you.

00:01:53.743 --> 00:01:55.905
And, much more important than
what anybody's opinion of you

00:01:55.905 --> 00:01:58.264
is is what is your opinion of yourself.

00:01:58.264 --> 00:02:01.062
If you can create the
environment and the routine

00:02:01.062 --> 00:02:03.852
and the regimen and
the schedule to believe

00:02:03.852 --> 00:02:08.019
that the crazy idea that you
have in here is possible,

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.410
then will align everything in
your life to make it happen.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.707
If you believe you're
going to go off and build

00:02:14.707 --> 00:02:17.644
a million dollar company
and you believe it,

00:02:17.644 --> 00:02:20.493
then it doesn't matter what
everybody else around you says.

00:02:20.493 --> 00:02:22.552
And they laugh at your lack of experience

00:02:22.552 --> 00:02:24.496
and they laugh at the idea
and they laugh at everything

00:02:24.496 --> 00:02:26.030
that's coming out of your
mouth, it doesn't matter,

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.336
'cause you believe it.

00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:29.008
And so, that's the most important thing.

00:02:29.008 --> 00:02:31.441
It doesn't matter what the
people around you are saying,

00:02:31.441 --> 00:02:33.630
what matters is what
you're saying to yourself.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.888
And I get that often that's a battle.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.258
One day you're energized

00:02:37.258 --> 00:02:38.668
and you're telling yourself
you can do anything,

00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:40.858
and another day you're down on yourself.

00:02:40.858 --> 00:02:43.043
I think it's important
to be hard on yourself,

00:02:43.043 --> 00:02:45.046
but not to kick yourself down,

00:02:45.046 --> 00:02:47.160
but rather kick yourself forward.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.147
If you kick yourself down,
then you're just negative

00:02:49.147 --> 00:02:51.306
and I'm no good, I'm never
going to amount to anything,

00:02:51.306 --> 00:02:52.156
then you won't.

00:02:52.156 --> 00:02:54.029
But if you kick yourself
forward to say okay,

00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:56.128
this project wasn't good,
I know I can do better,

00:02:56.128 --> 00:02:58.391
I know I can work harder,
I know I have the ability

00:02:58.391 --> 00:03:00.680
to make something great
and that was just okay,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.641
and to work to achieve that goal,

00:03:02.641 --> 00:03:06.808
and to create that environment
so that every day you wake up

00:03:07.743 --> 00:03:12.376
and feel that that big
goal you have is possible.

00:03:12.376 --> 00:03:14.058
Because people have done it.

00:03:14.058 --> 00:03:17.913
People who look like
you, with less resources,

00:03:17.913 --> 00:03:20.278
have gone on and done amazing things.

00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:22.223
There's no excuse why you can't go out

00:03:22.223 --> 00:03:24.167
and do something equally amazing,

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:27.374
except the one that you
are telling yourself.

00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:31.179
So, the question really
today is what is the excuse

00:03:31.179 --> 00:03:34.887
you're telling yourself
about why it's not possible?

00:03:34.887 --> 00:03:36.315
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.409
super curious to find out.

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:39.495
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Linh Podetti.

00:03:39.495 --> 00:03:41.568
Linh, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:03:41.568 --> 00:03:44.548
Your One Word, it really,
really, really means a lot to me,

00:03:44.548 --> 00:03:47.048
and I hope you are enjoying the read.

00:03:47.048 --> 00:03:49.449
So, thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:03:49.449 --> 00:03:51.209
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:53.841
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:03:53.841 --> 00:03:55.083
and I'll see you guys again

00:03:55.083 --> 00:03:58.073
tomorrow morning for
another shot of Entspresso.

00:03:58.073 --> 00:04:00.990
(upbeat rap music)

00:04:06.657 --> 00:04:08.786
- I want you to look
at something right now,

00:04:08.786 --> 00:04:10.584
think of some major goal you want,

00:04:10.584 --> 00:04:13.195
or maybe just one you're
already working on,

00:04:13.195 --> 00:04:15.681
and you have experienced
a lot of setbacks,

00:04:15.681 --> 00:04:17.222
a lot of defeats.

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:19.399
You've experienced a
lot of disappointment.

00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:21.499
Maybe you've already given up.

00:04:21.499 --> 00:04:24.303
And maybe you just need
a little encouragement

00:04:24.303 --> 00:04:26.008
to get back in the game again.

00:04:26.008 --> 00:04:28.328
Here's what I want you to look at:

00:04:28.328 --> 00:04:32.273
there are winners, and there are losers,

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:36.751
and there are people who have
not discovered how to win.

00:04:36.751 --> 00:04:39.283
And all they need is some coaching,

00:04:39.283 --> 00:04:42.026
all they need is some help and assistance,

00:04:42.026 --> 00:04:44.052
just a little support.

00:04:44.052 --> 00:04:46.151
All they need is some insight,

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:47.848
or different strategy or plan of action

00:04:47.848 --> 00:04:50.458
to make some adjustments that will open up

00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:52.657
the key to a whole new future for them.

00:04:52.657 --> 00:04:55.262
That will give them access
to the unlimited power

00:04:55.262 --> 00:04:59.098
that they have within themselves,
that's all that they need.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:02.830
So, what I want you to do
is think about something

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.654
you want for you that's real for you,

00:05:06.654 --> 00:05:09.061
that's important for you,

00:05:09.061 --> 00:05:12.911
that will give your life some
special meaning and power.

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:15.986
And I don't even want
you to say I can do that,

00:05:15.986 --> 00:05:18.291
I don't want you to assume that.

00:05:18.291 --> 00:05:20.821
See, five years ago when I
started out in this area,

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:24.081
I would not have been able
to make the mental leap

00:05:24.081 --> 00:05:27.804
that I would be up to
where I am right now.

00:05:27.804 --> 00:05:31.721
I don't want you to begin
to just psych yourself out.

00:05:31.721 --> 00:05:34.820
No, no, I want you to be able
to say something to yourself

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.985
that will enable you to
maintain a level of integrity

00:05:37.985 --> 00:05:40.334
with yourself, that when you say this,

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.752
even when you face tremendous setbacks,

00:05:42.752 --> 00:05:45.821
it will be a benchmark
to keep you in the game,

00:05:45.821 --> 00:05:48.740
to keep you moving
forward and experimenting

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.605
and readjusting your strategy,
and your plan of action

00:05:51.605 --> 00:05:55.103
continuously looking for ways to win.

00:05:55.103 --> 00:05:57.279
So, what is that something?

00:05:57.279 --> 00:05:59.152
When you got an idea you
might want to move on,

00:05:59.152 --> 00:06:00.226
you might not have the money,

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.032
you might not have the education,

00:06:02.032 --> 00:06:04.704
you might not have the support
or the resources you need.

00:06:04.704 --> 00:06:08.608
What is that something
that can keep us going,

00:06:08.608 --> 00:06:11.241
that will enable us to act on our dream?

00:06:11.241 --> 00:06:15.390
What's one of those keys
that will begin to help us

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.224
to discover the secrets to our dream?

00:06:18.224 --> 00:06:20.227
Here's what I want you to
repeat after me, please,

00:06:20.227 --> 00:06:22.890
with power and conviction,
say it's possible.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.818
- [Audience] It's possible.

00:06:24.818 --> 00:06:27.340
- That's all I want you to do
when you look at your dream,

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:30.837
you say to yourself
every day it's possible.

00:06:30.837 --> 00:06:34.177
You say that every day to
yourself, it's possible.

00:06:34.177 --> 00:06:35.428
Because what does that do?

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:39.095
See, it begins to change
your belief system.

00:06:40.323 --> 00:06:43.292
See, the way in which we
operate, ladies and gentlemen,

00:06:43.292 --> 00:06:45.629
is a manifestation of what we believe

00:06:45.629 --> 00:06:47.997
what's possible for us.

00:06:47.997 --> 00:06:49.639
Whatever you've done up to this point,

00:06:49.639 --> 00:06:54.477
all that it really is is a
duplication, it's a reproduction,

00:06:54.477 --> 00:06:57.455
of what you belief self
consciously that you deserve,

00:06:57.455 --> 00:06:59.532
and what's possible for your life.

00:06:59.532 --> 00:07:03.699
Before April, 1954, the common
belief, the universal belief,

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.664
because it had been tried
again and again and again,

00:07:09.664 --> 00:07:13.085
and people felt the belief
was that man was not

00:07:13.085 --> 00:07:17.829
physically capable of breaking
the four minute barrier,

00:07:17.829 --> 00:07:21.514
that he could not run a mile
in less than four minutes.

00:07:21.514 --> 00:07:26.351
That was the belief on the
planet, it had never been done.

00:07:26.351 --> 00:07:29.475
But here's what happened,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:07:29.475 --> 00:07:31.893
Roger Bannister came along,

00:07:31.893 --> 00:07:34.976
and he broke the four minute barrier.

00:07:36.369 --> 00:07:38.847
Now, here's what's significant about that.

00:07:38.847 --> 00:07:41.883
Since that time, up to this day,

00:07:41.883 --> 00:07:46.050
over 20,000 people have done
it, including high school kids.

00:07:49.413 --> 00:07:52.913
What changed? 20,000 people, what changed?

00:07:54.082 --> 00:07:56.758
Here's what happened when
they got on the track:

00:07:56.758 --> 00:07:59.565
they knew it had been done,

00:07:59.565 --> 00:08:01.621
and because they knew it had been done,

00:08:01.621 --> 00:08:04.933
there was a new belief about this barrier,

00:08:04.933 --> 00:08:08.016
about this goal that was unreachable.

00:08:08.964 --> 00:08:13.584
And those 20,000 people
got in the race believing,

00:08:13.584 --> 00:08:15.632
knowing in their heart
that someone had done it,

00:08:15.632 --> 00:08:18.983
that it's possible that they could do it.

00:08:18.983 --> 00:08:21.475
And I'm saying that if you know
anybody that had some goal,

00:08:21.475 --> 00:08:24.751
some dream, something
that they wanted to do

00:08:24.751 --> 00:08:27.680
and they did it, then
I'm saying that you know

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.548
in your heart that if someone has done it,

00:08:30.548 --> 00:08:33.367
then you can do it, it's possible.

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:35.816
And in fact, if someone
can make their dream

00:08:35.816 --> 00:08:38.107
become a reality, then it's possible

00:08:38.107 --> 00:08:40.987
that you can make your
dream become reality.

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.276
- [Voiceover] In only 21 years,

00:08:42.276 --> 00:08:43.963
Koenigsegg has come from nowhere

00:08:43.963 --> 00:08:46.726
to be one of the highest
regarded hyper car manufacturers,

00:08:46.726 --> 00:08:50.524
being counted alongside Ferrari,
Lamborghini, and McLaren.

00:08:50.524 --> 00:08:52.491
How have they pulled that off?

00:08:52.491 --> 00:08:55.595
- Well, we had to work
hard, being innovative,

00:08:55.595 --> 00:08:59.762
and don't believe in the
hype that it's impossible.

00:09:00.732 --> 00:09:03.800
But it's, you know, every day we strive

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.217
and push and learn and adapt,

00:09:07.809 --> 00:09:11.378
and when you do that for
20 years with a great focus

00:09:11.378 --> 00:09:15.166
within the group, you can
do pretty much anything,

00:09:15.166 --> 00:09:16.810
I think that's the simple answer.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.830
But for sure, it's not easy,

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.825
you have to be prepared
to work hard for it.

